                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>What is The Souled Store's biggest moat?</h3>
                                        <p>Legal IP licensing partnerships (Marvel, Disney, IPL, F1, Harry Potter etc.) create instant brand equity + built-in fandom incumbents can't replicate.</p>
                                        <h3>Can smaller brands do licensed IP?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes for smaller / niche IPs (regional cricket, indie music, gaming, anime). Global blockbuster IP requires larger commitment.</p>
                                        <h3>Should I focus on one fandom or many?</h3>
                                        <p>Depth per fandom > breadth. TSS added fandoms only after establishing category leadership in each.</p>
                                        <h3>Is IP licensing expensive?</h3>
                                        <p>Varies enormously by IP + region + royalty structure. Global blockbusters: significant royalty + minimum guarantee. Regional / niche IP: often reasonable.</p>
